    <li><span class="when">Startup</span><div><b>CTO &amp; co-founder</b> of <a href="https://medium.com/@sellarafaeli/yes-no-architecture-of-a-social-network-startup-in-2016-d6d2989ca1b3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">yes.no</a>, a Q&amp;A social network.</div></li>
    <li><span class="when">Industry</span><div><b>Many dev roles</b> at orgs of every size, in San Francisco and Tel Aviv, Fiverr among them.</div></li>
    <li><span class="when">Degree</span><div><b>BSc Computer Science &amp; Psychology</b>, Hebrew University, <i>magna cum laude</i>.</div></li>
    <li><span class="when">Army</span><div><b>Intelligence Officer</b>, five years in Israel's SIGINT unit, 8200.</div></li>
    <li><span class="when">Travel</span><div><b>A year backpacking</b> South America, and <a href="/about">a lot of other adventures</a>.</div></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="aside">Fond of vanilla JS, Ruby (Sinatra) and MongoDB. Building complex web apps single-handedly has been the thread through all of it.</p>
</section>

